1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,409
You see, remember, the slope is
equal to the thermal expansion

2
00:00:08,409 --> 00:00:11,712
coefficient--

3
00:00:11,712 --> 00:00:15,015
thermal expansion coefficient.

4
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:18,385
And those slopes are the same
for the different glasses.

5
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:21,321
Just because I've
cooled one differently,

6
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:23,123
they're not going to
have different slopes.

7
00:00:23,123 --> 00:00:26,026
And this is the
fundamental challenge.

8
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,761
This is the fundamental
confusion point

9
00:00:27,761 --> 00:00:31,799
that happens which is
that this is not time.

10
00:00:31,799 --> 00:00:35,302
This axis is not time.

11
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:41,575
So this is wrong to.

12
00:00:41,575 --> 00:00:44,878
What we're doing is we're
talking about something

13
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,648
involving time, cooling rate.

14
00:00:47,648 --> 00:00:49,883
But we're plotting
it on something

15
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:52,553
that doesn't involve time, and
that can lead to confusion.

16
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:53,921
So I wanted to point that out.

17
00:00:53,921 --> 00:00:55,355
You say, well,
shouldn't the slope

18
00:00:55,355 --> 00:00:58,125
be different because you're
cooling it slower or faster?

19
00:00:58,125 --> 00:01:00,060
No, that's not
what this slope is.

20
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,429
This slope is a thermal
expansion coefficient.

21
00:01:02,429 --> 00:01:06,600
So the right answer
to this must be

22
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:13,707
that you have your
nice liquid phase

23
00:01:13,707 --> 00:01:16,844
and you've made
your two glasses.

24
00:01:16,844 --> 00:01:19,480
So here's one.

25
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,850
This has cooled faster.

26
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:23,484
This is slower.

27
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:29,356
This would be Tg.

28
00:01:29,356 --> 00:01:34,528
This would be another
Tg, maybe Tg1, Tg2.

29
00:01:34,528 --> 00:01:41,201
And the Tm would
come down and have--

30
00:01:41,201 --> 00:01:44,638
well, I've run out
of room here, but Tm

31
00:01:44,638 --> 00:01:46,573
might come down like this.

32
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:49,543
And so T1 must be
somewhere up here.
